Template search 1 gave mapped_rxn and template_id 29646. Apply_template-1 gave three possible precursors (list of lists). Those are three possible sets? Actually each inner list is a list of SMILES strings (maybe multiple precursors). For template 1, each list contains one SMILES? Actually answer: '[["C/C(=C/[C@H]1O[C@@H](C/C=C/C=C/C(=O)O[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C)C[C@H](O)[C@H]1C)CO"], ["C/C(=C/[C@H]1O[C@@H](C/C=C/C=C/C(=O)O)C[C@H](O[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C)[C@H]1C)CO"], ["C/C(=C/[C@H]1O[C@@H](C/C=C/C=C/C(=O)O)C[C@H](O)[C@H]1C)CO[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C"]]' So three possible precursors each single molecule (maybe the protected vs deprotected). So step1: target molecule is something with TBS group? The reaction is deprotection? The forward reaction: TBS protecting group introduced, forward breaks O-Si bond? Actually description: TBS introduced using TBDMSCl, bond O-Si formed. In retrosynthesis we break O-Si to get alcohol precursor. So target is TBS-protected molecule. The precursors are the deprotected alcohol (maybe plus TBDMSCl). But the precursors list only includes one SMILES each, maybe the alcohol only (the other reagent omitted). So we need to construct route: target molecule (the protected) -> reaction (template_id 29646) -> precursor molecule (the deprotected). Then further steps: apply_template-2 etc.

But we have multiple transformations: template 2 (HWE) with template_id 74197, precursors list: two SMILES: ['C/C(=C/[C@H]1O[C@@H](C/C=C/C=O)C[C@H](O)[C@H]1C)CO', 'COP(=O)(CC(=O)O[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C)OC'] So that step likely splits target into two fragments: an aldehyde/ketone and a phosphonate ester.

Template 3 (DIBAL-H reduction) with template_id 1037371, precursors list: one SMILES: ['C/C(=C/[C@H]1O[C@@H](C/C=C/C=O)C[C@H](OC(=O)/C=C/C=C/C=C/C=C/C(=O)O)[C@H]1C)CO'].

Template 4 (TMS protection) with template_id 185267, precursors list: two SMILES: ["C/C(=C/[C@H]1O[C@@H](C/C=C/C=O)C[C@H](O)[C@H]1C)CO", "CCC(CC)C(=O)OC(=O)/C=C/C=C/C=C/C=C/C(=O)O"].

Template 5 had no mapping, empty.

